ow sequence. It creates a definitive 4-in-a-row threat, forcing the opponent into a defensive move at N4. This keeps the initiative with White and advances the board state favorably.\n\nReason: Extending the diagonal line J8-K7-L6 to M5 creates an immediate win threat (4-in-a-row). Since the opponent must block this threat immediately, White controls the tempo of the game.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "M", "row": 5}'}
